ive label), was acquired by BMG. Two years later, the label became part of the newly formed [l=Zomba Label Group], a unit of [l=Sony BMG Music Entertainment]. From 2008 to 2011, it was part of the Jive Label Group (also known as the [l=RCA/Jive Label Group]) under [l=Sony Music].\n\nOn September 26, 2011, while a certainty of Jive's artists migrated to sister label [l=Epic], the [l=RCA Music Group] was disbanded by [l=Sony], and on October 7, Jive, alongside sister labels [l=Arista], [l=LaFace Records] and [l=J Records], were all absorbed into [l=RCA Records], bringing all of its artists to the RCA family.\n\nThe Jive label would later be relaunched in January 2020 as a division of Sony Music Entertainment Italy, releasing hip hop/R&B/pop from up-and-coming Italian artists. The label's relaunch was led by Antonio Dikele Distefano, founder and editor of Esse Magazine.\n\nOn 3rd February 2026, RCA Records announced the re-launch of the iconic label JIVE Records as a stand alone worldwide label under the direction of Mike Weiss & David Melhado. Jive will operate out of Sony Music’s New York City headquarters with Mike Weiss & David Melhado reporting to RCA Records Chairman and CEO, Peter Edge & COO, John Fleckenstein.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:2186","relations":{"parentLabel":{"id":264083,"name":"Sony Music Entertainment Germany GmbH"},"sublabels":[{"id":106977,"name":"$hort Records"},{"id":761893,"name":"2Morro Music"},{"id":14779,"name":"Battery Records"},{"id":164537,"name":"Dance Jive"},{"id":28478,"name":"Dangerous Music"},{"id":277746,"name":"Hitz Committee"},{"id":63244,"name":"Jive Afrika"},{"id":1443751,"name":"Jive Chicago"},{"id":399855,"name":"Jive Classic 12\" Series"},{"id":432,"name":"Jive Electro"},{"id":154246,"name":"Jive House"},{"id":389087,"name":"Jive Jazz Collection"},{"id":1928768,"name":"Jive Legacy"},{"id":35555,"name":"Mojo Records"},{"id":1274,"name":"Pepper Records"},{"id":1530200,"name":"Soul Searching (3)"},{"id":579193,"